# #1597. The Vercel project's Root Directory is `site`, but the CLI uploads the directory it is
# RUN FROM — so `vercel deploy` now runs from the repo root and this file decides what leaves the
# machine. Without it the whole 40M / ~2000-file repo would be uploaded on every deploy, including
# report-template/findings.*.json (real client engagement data) and targets/** (vendored apps).
#
# Allowlist, not denylist: a new top-level directory is EXCLUDED by default, so adding one cannot
# silently start shipping. `src` is here deliberately — it is what makes the site able to import
# shared logic (site/app/supabase-security-checker/page.tsx -> src/supabase-write-probe.ts) instead
# of keeping a relocated copy. The three root manifests are what pnpm needs to resolve the
# workspace; the build fails loudly, not silently, if any is missing.
/*
!/site
!/src
!/package.json
!/pnpm-lock.yaml
!/pnpm-workspace.yaml

# Build output and local env inside the allowlisted dirs.
site/.next
site/node_modules
